---
/*
 * Analyst attention — B2B 상품 지면. (seoulmarkets.com/data/analyst-attention)
 *
 * 왜 (사장님 데이터 상품 사업): 대형 벤더가 파는 것은 「리포트 그 자체」다. 우리가 파는 것은
 *   「관심이 어디에 쏠리고 어디가 비는가」 — 소수 종목에 리서치가 얼마나 몰리나. 퀀트·팩터·
 *   미디어·IR 이 산다. ⛔ 값은 지면에 안 넣는다(사장님 확정 대기). 결제 안 붙인다 — 살 뜻만 센다.
 *
 * ⚠ 정직 관문: 우리 아카이브는 한 묶음 증권사의 소매 리서치 「표본」이다. 어떤 회사가 안 뜬 것은
 *   「우리 표본에 안 떴다」이지 「시장이 그 회사를 안 본다」가 아니다. 이 문장을 화면에 못박는다.
 *   그래서 각도가 「커버리지 사막」이 아니라 「관심 쏠림」이다.
 *
 * 자료: src/data/analyst-coverage.json (scripts/build-analyst-coverage.mjs 산출).
 *   리서치 원본의 티커 필드가 성겨서(6,372건 중 352건) 종목명으로 이었다 — 그 단서를 화면에 적는다.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../consts';
import data from '../../data/analyst-coverage.json';

const s = data.summary;
const rows = data.by_sector;
const TITLE = 'Where analyst attention piles up';
const SAMPLE = `${s.total_stock_reports.toLocaleString()} single-stock reports · ${data.brokerages_in_archive} brokerages · ${s.year}`;
const DESC =
  'Korean equity research attention by sector, from our archive of single-stock broker reports: how '
  + 'many listed companies drew a report, how heavily attention concentrates, and where it thins out.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Korean analyst attention by sector',
  description: DESC, url: `${SITE_URL}/data/analyst-attention`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SeoulMarkets', url: SITE_URL },
  variableMeasured: ['companies drawing a report', 'reports per company', 'attention concentration by sector'],
};
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="pp">
      <p class="kicker">SeoulMarkets · data for licence</p>
      <h1>Where analyst attention piles up</h1>
      <p class="sample">{SAMPLE}</p>
      <p class="lead">
        Korean brokerages write a lot of research — and it lands on the same few names. From our
        archive of single-stock reports we measure <b>where attention concentrates and where it
        thins</b>: {s.covered.toLocaleString()} of {s.listed_companies.toLocaleString()} listed
        companies drew at least one report in {s.year}; the busiest name drew {s.busiest_report_count};
        the median covered company drew {s.median_reports_when_covered}.
      </p>

      <aside class="caveat" role="note">
        <b>Read this first.</b> This is an archive of retail-board research from {data.brokerages_in_archive}
        brokerages — a sample, not the whole market. A company <b>not appearing</b> means it drew no
        report <i>in this sample</i>; it is <b>not</b> a claim that no analyst covers it, and it is
        neither a buy nor a sell signal. What the data measures is <b>attention concentration</b>, not
        market-wide coverage.
      </aside>

      <ol class="five">
        <li><b>What it is</b> — for each sector, how many of its listed companies appeared in analyst
          research this year, how many reports they drew, and how many drew just one.</li>
        <li><b>Why trust it</b> — every report is a filed, dated broker note we archived, joined to a
          company by name and to our public-code sector scheme.</li>
        <li><b>How big</b> — {s.total_stock_reports.toLocaleString()} single-stock reports across
          {s.distinct_names_in_research.toLocaleString()} named companies in {s.year}.</li>
        <li><b>The honest caveat</b> — the ticker field is filled on only a fraction of reports (a
          scraper gap), so coverage is joined by <b>company name</b>; and the archive is a sample of
          brokerages, so absence is not market-wide.</li>
        <li><b>The form</b> — one CSV: sector · listed companies · companies with a report · coverage
          share · reports · companies with only one report. Plus the concentration summary.</li>
      </ol>

      <section class="blk">
        <h2>① Attention, by sector</h2>
        <p>The share of each sector's listed companies that drew at least one report this year. It runs
          from the low twenties to the high thirties — and even the covered names are thin: hundreds
          drew a single report all year.</p>
        <table class="press">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Sector</th><th class="r">Listed</th><th class="r">With a report</th>
              <th class="r">Share</th><th class="r">Reports</th><th class="r">One only</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="axis">{r.sector}</td>
                <td class="r">{r.listed}</td>
                <td class="r">{r.covered}</td>
                <td class="r"><b>{r.coverage_pct}%</b></td>
                <td class="r">{r.reports.toLocaleString()}</td>
                <td class="r">{r.thin_one_report_only}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="fine">
          Across the market, {s.one_report_only.toLocaleString()} companies drew exactly one report all
          year, and {s.single_house.toLocaleString()} were seen by a single brokerage. Attention is not
          spread — it stacks on a short list while most of the market goes unwritten-about in this
          sample.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="blk">
        <h2>② What you get</h2>
        <table class="kv">
          <tbody>
            <tr><th>Files</th><td colspan="2">One CSV — sector · listed companies · companies with a
              report · coverage share · report count · companies with only one report. Plus the
              market-wide concentration summary.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>The join</th><td colspan="2">By <b>company name</b>: the raw ticker field is present
              on only {s.total_stock_reports > 0 ? '352' : 'a fraction'} of {s.total_stock_reports.toLocaleString()}
              reports — a scraper gap, not a market fact. Every uncoded report still names one stock.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>The sample</th><td colspan="2">Retail-board research from {data.brokerages_in_archive}
              brokerages. Absence means "not in this sample", never "market-wide uncovered".</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Refresh</th><td colspan="2">Daily archive; the panel rolls up the current year.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Source</th><td colspan="2">Our own daily archive of broker research boards, joined to
              KRX names and our public-KSIC sector scheme.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="cta">
        <h2>Ask for the dataset</h2>
        <p class="cta__lead">
          Want the by-sector attention panel, or the concentration series over time? Leave a work email
          and we send a sample and the current licensing terms. It reaches us directly — no account, and
          this is not the newsletter.
        </p>
        <form class="ask" method="post" action="/v1/subscribe" data-source="analyst-attention">
          <label class="vh" for="ask-email">Work email</label>
          <div class="ask__row">
            <input id="ask-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
              inputmode="email" placeholder="you@company.com" aria-describedby="ask-note" />
            <button type="submit">Request the dataset</button>
          </div>
          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="ask-hp">Leave this field empty</label>
            <input id="ask-hp" type="text" name="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <p class="ask__note" id="ask-note">We store your address and that you asked about the analyst
            attention dataset. We never sell or share it.</p>
          <p class="ask__msg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </section>

      <p class="fine bottom">
        From our own broker-research archive · Joined by company name (ticker-field gap) · A brokerage
        sample, so absence is not market-wide · Not investment advice. See our{' '}
        <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> and <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const form = document.querySelector('form.ask');
      if (!form) return;
      const input = form.querySelector('input[name="email"]');
      const hp = form.querySelector('input[name="hp"]');
      const btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
      const msg = form.querySelector('.ask__msg');
      const say = (state, text) => { msg.dataset.state = state; msg.textContent = text; };
      form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const email = input.value.trim();
        if (!email) return;
        btn.disabled = true; const was = btn.textContent; btn.textContent = 'Sending…';
        delete msg.dataset.state;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/v1/subscribe', {
            method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ email, hp: hp.value, source: form.dataset.source || 'analyst-attention' }),
          });
          const d = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
          if (res.ok && d.ok) { say('ok', 'Thanks — we have your address and will email you the sample and the terms.'); form.reset(); }
          else { say('error', d?.error?.message || d?.message || 'Could not send. Please try again.'); }
        } catch { say('error', 'Network error. Please try again.'); }
        finally { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = was; }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

<style>
  .pp { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .kicker { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700; margin: 1.2rem 0 .3rem; }
  .pp h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .pp .sample { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
                margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .pp .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
  .pp .lead b { font-weight: 650; }
  .caveat { margin: 0 0 1.8rem; padding: .9rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--accent);
            border-radius: 8px; background: var(--accent-soft, var(--card)); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .caveat b { color: var(--ink); }
  .five { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.1rem 2.4rem; background: var(--card);
          border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }
  .five li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .five li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .five li b { color: var(--ink); }
  .blk { margin: 0 0 2.2rem; }
  .blk h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .blk p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  table.kv, table.press { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .9rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  table.kv th, table.kv td, table.press th, table.press td {
    padding: .55rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  table.kv th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; width: 1%; }
  table.kv td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.kv td[colspan] { white-space: normal; line-height: 1.6; font-variant-numeric: normal; }
  table.press th { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
                   color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  table.press td.axis { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  .r { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  code { font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: .86em;
         background: var(--card); padding: .1em .35em; border-radius: 4px; }
  .cta { margin: 2.4rem 0 0; padding: 1.3rem 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--line);
         border-radius: 10px; background: var(--card); }
  .cta h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .cta p { line-height: 1.7; font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta__lead { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cta a, .pp a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; padding-bottom: 1px; }
  .cta a:hover, .pp a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .vh { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  .ask__row { display: flex; gap: .5rem; max-width: 30rem; }
  .ask__row input { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; font: inherit; font-size: .95rem; padding: .6rem .7rem;
    color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .ask__row button { flex: 0 0 auto; font: inherit; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
    padding: .6rem 1rem; color: var(--bg); background: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row button:hover { opacity: .9; }
  .ask__row button[disabled] { opacity: .6; cursor: default; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
  .ask__note { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .ask__msg { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.55; display: none; }
  .ask__msg[data-state] { display: block; }
  .ask__msg[data-state='ok'] { color: var(--up, #1a7f37); }
  .ask__msg[data-state='error'] { color: var(--down, #c0392b); }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) { .ask__row { flex-direction: column; } .ask__row button { width: 100%; } }
  .fine { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .fine.bottom { margin: 2.4rem 0 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { table.kv th { white-space: normal; } .pp .sample { white-space: normal; } }
</style>
